flowchart TB
accTitle: Pending work drives worker capacity
accDescr: S3 stores objects while SQS stores work references. A feedback loop divides visible backlog by active workers and adjusts the fleet toward a latency-derived target.
S[(S3 images and results)]:::storage <-->|Read input, write output| W[Auto Scaling workers]:::output
Q[(SQS object keys)]:::storage -->|Claim job, acknowledge success| W
Q -.->|Visible backlog| M[Backlog / in-service workers]:::decision
W -.->|Worker count| M
T[Target = acceptable delay<br/>/ average job time]:::inputData --> M
M -.->|Adjust desired capacity| W
Q -->|Repeated failures| D[(Dead-letter queue<br/>Investigate and redrive)]:::warning
